{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For the chief musician. In You, YHWH, I have taken refuge; let me never be put to shame.</b> — They gave it to one of the musicians to play." "<b>In You</b> — the meaning: for my enemies are men of violence against me without cause."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:00.518847091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}